1. WHAT RECORD l9stk STATES OF G2 (RECORD: its l9stk_guard.out and page 15.9 at 43da41ca, copied)
   the 130 C preset: no trip under 127.8 C, surely tripped from 132.2 C, resets between 122.3 and 127.7 C
   margins: 38.4 K at 10 A (junction 89.4 C), 9.8 K in the 18 A service (118.0 C); at the gauge's condition C4 (121.8 C) 6.0 K
   the gradient left on the worst split 15.68 K (two FETs carrying all 13.56 K); the junction's lead 2.12 K (4.24 K), Rth(j-mb) 1.4 K/W
   the guard's draw 18.25 uA against 30 uA; the regulator in regulation from BRK_VIN 9.68 V; the shunt's off leakage 5 uA at 55 C
     PRINTED, 43.6 uA at 86.25 C ASSUMED, counted on the return
   its predicate: "the loop with the fixed resistor keeps the first inverter on, the held reading, the window and the gates at
     every voltage: yes"; its acceptance (c): "so a ramping loop (a docking, the gauge's wake, a back-fed precharge) is never
     read held"; its window check: "RET/OUT closed 0.590 against 0.4603" (the closed loop's ratio)

2. THE SWITCH ON ITS SHEET: TI LM26LV, SNIS144G (July 2007, revised September 2016); held back
   PRINTED: trip point accuracy -2.2 to +2.2 C at TA 0 to 150 C and VDD = 5 V (6.8; the only condition it is printed at)
     the 130 C preset: no trip under 127.8 C, surely tripped from 132.2 C; hysteresis 4.5 to 5.5 C (6.6, over VDD 1.6 to 5.5 V and -50 to
     150 C): resets between 122.3 and 127.7 C                                                     record l9stk's figures: REPRODUCED
   PRINTED: supply 1.6 to 5.5 V recommended, 6 V absolute; IS 16 uA at most over -50 to 150 C and 1.6 to 5.5 V; TJ(MAX) 155 C
   PRINTED: OVERTEMP (pin 5) active high, push-pull: VOH at least VDD - 0.2 V sourcing up to 780 uA (VDD 3.3 V or more); VOL at most
     0.2 V sinking up to 385 uA; the open-drain output (pin 3) is active LOW and needs a pull-up: it is not the one to use
   PRINTED: outputs enabled 2.3 ms at most after VDD passes 1.3 V (tEN); their state before that is NOT PRINTED (taken as high, the
     worse side for a false hold); TRIP_TEST asserts both outputs, read high from VDD - 0.5 V, 2.5 uA at most into it, and puts VTRIP
     on VTEMP: 0.958 V for a 130 C preset (Table 1, gain 4: a check in place that the part is the 130 C preset)
   PRINTED: the thermal pad may float (for noise, to ground); RthJA 100.7 C/W: its own heating at 5 V and 16 uA 0.008 K (DERIVED)
   orderable table: LM26LVQISDX-130/NOPB Active; LM26LVQISD-130/NOPB Obsolete; LM26LVCISD-125/NOPB Active                REPRODUCED
   NOT PRINTED: the trip point at any VDD but 5 V; record l9stk writes "at a 5 V supply", which is the condition, not a range

3. THE REGULATOR ON ITS SHEET: TI TPS70950 (TPS709 family, SBVS186H, March 2012, revised July 2021); held back
   PRINTED: input 2.7 to 30 V recommended, 32 V absolute, against the loop's 29.2 V clamp: holds; TJ recommended to 125 C
   PRINTED: the table's conditions are TA -40 to +85 C, VIN = VOUT(typ) + 1 V (6.0 V here), IOUT = 1 mA "unless otherwise noted"
     DC accuracy +-1 % (VOUT 3.3 V or more): 4.95 to 5.05 V; line regulation 10 mV at most from 6.0 to 30 V; load regulation 50 mV
     at most from 100 uA to 150 mA; dropout 500 mV at most at 50 mA (TPS70950); start 1.5 ms at most (VOUT over 3.3 V, 47 ohm load)
     ground current 2.25 uA at most at IOUT = 0 (VOUT over 3.3 V), at the table's VIN of 6.0 V: NOT PRINTED at 7.6 V (in dropout),
     10.6, 16.8 or 29.2 V. TYPICAL: Figure 6-15 (the TPS70933, EN open) draws it flat at about 1.3, 1.75 and 2.25 uA (-40, 25,
     85 C) from about 8 V to 30 V; Figure 6-16 rises by microamps per milliampere of load; the dropout's ground current is described
     ("limits the increase") and not printed (read on the page image by this record; TYPICAL, not a limit)
   PRINTED: EN may float (a 300 nA pull-up; never tied to IN, its 6.5 V clamp); COUT 1.5 uF effective or more, ESR 0.2 ohm or less;
     an input capacitor is needed for line transients over 10 V (DOCK_EN_OUT steps from 0 to the loop's level at every docking)
   the guard's input current at the switch's 16 uA: 18.25 uA PRINTED at VIN 6.0 V and IOUT 1 mA's table (record l9stk's 18.25 uA:
     REPRODUCED as a figure; its conditions are the table's, so at the loop's voltages it is the TYPICAL curve's, inside the 30 uA
     allowance with 11.75 uA to spare); the output at 16 uA is under the load regulation's printed 100 uA: its accuracy there NOT PRINTED
   the dropout at the guard's microamps: not printed; 7.3.2 says it "approximately scales with the output current" (a description, not a
     limit), so the printed 500 mV at 50 mA is a bound there (record l9stk takes it so)
   the regulation threshold: record l9stk takes VOUT + 1 % + the dropout bound, 5.55 V on DOCK_EN_OUT; the table's own condition for
     the printed accuracy is VIN at least 6.0 V

