       Tripped, it meets it from 10.45 V; under that the switch holds its output on less than 5 V (it runs from 1.6 V), so the RESET
       point after a trip below 10.45 V is not printed; the next trip, with the loop closed again, is (a restart point, not the protection)
   (e) THE WINDOW (L4-E11 20c: "A ramping closed loop never reads held while RT1 is under 25.8 kOhm (RET/OUT over 0.4603 when OUT
       reads powered)"; "a trigger there stops a dead pack's precharge"). Board A reads OUT powered from 1.825 V at least (1.981 V at most)
       and RET held under 0.7755 V at least (closed over 0.84 V at most); a ramp is never read held only if RET stays over 0.84 V
       wherever OUT reaches 1.825 V. 25.8 kOhm is a ratio bound (22 / (22 + RT1) at 0.4603): it counts no sink on the return.
