7. VERDICT AND THE STOP
   NOT CONFIRMED, one figure: G2 as selected (the AO3400A on DOCK_EN_RET, the fixed 15 kOhm) keeps L4-E11 20c's window only while the
   shunt's site stays under 77.9 C on the assumed doubling; at record l9stk's own 86.25 C site the sinks on the return are 45.7 uA against
   the 26.4 uA the window allows, and a ramping closed loop reads held (finding L8P-F08, OPEN). Every other figure of record l9stk this
   script reads REPRODUCES (sections 2 to 6), with three relabellings: the trip accuracy is printed at VDD 5 V only; the regulator's
   ground current is printed at the table's VIN 6.0 V only (TYPICAL elsewhere); its accuracy is printed from 100 uA of load.
   As the brief orders, the draft STOPS here: no apply script is written for G2 in this round (a negative check of this solution, the
   first). L8P-F07 stays OPEN.
   The smallest correction scope for the selection's owner (DERIVED, NOT DRAFTED, NOT CHECKED; one of these, each a material change):
     (i)   a shunt of lower leakage: the kit's 2N7002 (Q44's and Q107's part) prints IDSS 80 nA at 60 V (25 C); on the same doubling
           5.58 uA at 86.25 C, 7.7 uA on the return in all against 26.4 uA; its on-resistance is printed at VGS 5 V (7 ohm at most) and 10 V
           only, where the switch drives 4.75 V: tripped, the return 16.5 mV at 29.2 V with 14 ohm hot (a bound under 5 V, ASSUMED)
     (ii)  the fixed resistor at most 11.57 kOhm nominal with the AO3400A at 86.25 C (DERIVED, +1 %), 11 kOhm in E24: tripped, the regulator
           then meets the table's condition only from 11.93 V, over the pack's 10.6 V, so a trip low in the service holds on under 5 V
     (iii) the shunt's site bounded under 77.9 C (a layout condition, 1.6 K over the air), with the leakage's doubling still ASSUMED
   The trip and no-trip sides on the case row (section 6) do not depend on this choice.

